At time \(t=0\), a particle is represented by the wave function:
\[
\Psi(x,0)=\begin{cases}
A(x/a), & 0\le x\le a\\
A(b-x)/(b-a), & a\le x\le b\\
0, & \text{otherwise}
\end{cases}
\]
where \(A=3/b\), and \(a\) and \(b\) are (positive) constants. What is the probability of finding the particle to the left of \(a\)?

