where \(0<c<L\) and \(A=\dfrac{5}{L}\). What is the probability of finding the particle in the region \(x<c\)?

Consider a one-dimensional infinite square well of width \(L\):
\[
V(x)=\begin{cases}
0, & 0<x<L\\
\infty, & \text{otherwise.}
\end{cases}
\]
Inside the well define \(k^2\equiv 2mE/\hbar^2\).

